---
import Drawer from '@guillemservera/astro-drawer/Drawer.astro'
import DemoLayout from '../../layouts/DemoLayout.astro'
---

<DemoLayout title="Form drawer">
	<p>The form sits in <code>[data-drawer-no-drag]</code>, so it never starts a drag. <code>autoFocus</code> moves focus to the first control once the open transition is over (by default the sheet itself keeps it, like vue-drawer); <code>open-auto-focus</code> can cancel it. On iOS the sheet moves above the keyboard.</p>
	<button class="tap" id="open" data-drawer-open="#drawer">Create alert</button>
	<Drawer id="drawer" autoFocus aria-labelledby="form-title">
		<h2 id="form-title">Create alert</h2>
		<form data-drawer-no-drag onsubmit="event.preventDefault(); this.closest('astro-drawer').close()">
			<label>Symbol <input id="symbol" name="symbol" autocomplete="off" /></label>
			<label>Alert type
				<select name="type"><option>Breakout</option><option>Pullback</option><option>Volatility</option></select>
			</label>
			<button class="tap" type="submit">Save alert</button>
		</form>
	</Drawer>
</DemoLayout>
